      "{'text': 'If you want to prepare something easy and cute for your kids birthday, then you should definitely try some delicious mug recipes. Easy to make and kids will love it! Take a look at my favorite mug recipes for kids birthdays.\\nOf course, this is also perfect when you want to eat something sweet and don’t really have much time to cook!\\nI found this jar recipe on one amazing link party long time ago, and I knew immediately I have to save it on my list of easy birthday recipes for later! Tatanisha from A mitten full of saving has amazing recipes and this one will definitely be a huge hit with my family and friends.\\nLovely Stephanie from Spaceships and Laser beams blog made these amazing chocolate snickers mug cake. I think everyone would be so happy when I serve this. It looks amazing.\\nLolli from Food Fun Family shared this cool recipe with her readers. I knew this is one of the jar and mug recipes that I need to include in my roundup. It’s simple and so tasty – you need to check it out!\\nDawn from Blogging Mom of 4 blog shared this amazingly cool and simple paleo mug recipe on her blog and I knew that I have to save it for later. Chocolate is not really approved for paleo diet – but this cake will be like you’re eating a real choco cake!\\nMaryann from Domestically Speaking shared this amazing muffin mug recipe with her readers. And I am not the only one that liked it – it has so many shares on Pinterest that you can be sure it’s good!\\nBritannie from Simplistically Living shared this great recipe with her readers and I had to share it with mine! It’s not too complicated, and it looks more than tasty!\\nHere comes something simple and nice and just in time for Christmas. Lovely Brittanie (again) shared this on her blog and I just love love love it!\\nDo you like these delicious mug recipes? Which one is your favorite? Do you have your own recipe to share with me? Feel free to leave the link in the comment so I can check them out and add them to the list of mug recipes.\\nWell, you know what I think about cooking activities for kids – so invite your little ones to bake with you! Enjoy!', 'timestamp': '2019-04-18 11:02:19', 'url': 'https://www.parentaljourney.com/tag/jar-recipes/'}\n",
