      "{'text': 'I\\'ve always loved birth. My mom was a childbirth educator, so I was lucky enough to grow up with expectant parents practicing breathing techniques and birthing positions in our living room every Tuesday night. Becoming a doula was the most natural thing in the world for me, and I\\'ve loved every sweaty, beautiful second of it since I became a certified birth and postpartum doula in 2015.\\nAs part of the birth justice movement, I believe that all parents deserve an empowering and celebrated birth experience regardless of race, ethnicity, gender, class, sexuality, body type, or religion, and I am over-the-moon excited to work with you towards the birth experience you\\'re hoping for.\\nWhat is a doula, and do I really need one?\\nWhy should I use a Roots of Labor certified doula?\\n\"Her aura, presence, demeanor, whatever you want to call it is immediately and palpably calming. It\\'s the same way a puppy makes you smile without even thinking about it. She\\'s like a walking cup of chamomile tea.\"\\n\"Her hands-on comfort techniques, gentle affirmations, and calming presence were invaluable to me and I truly don\\'t know I could have had the birth experience I hoped for without her.\"\\n\"She made me feel safe and relaxed. She laughed with me and cheered us on. My mom told her, \\'You are part of the family now,\\' and it\\'s true.\"\\nI had difficulties finding a doula who was familiar with the LGBTQ scene enough to feel comfortable in my home. Keelia acquainted herself with everyone (and their pronouns) so she really felt like part of the family.\\n\"Keelia\\'s presence in the room and her counsel and good-nature kept us feeling empowered and focused. I cannot imagine the experience without her.\"\\nI will provide emotional, educational, and physical support to ease your pregnancy and empower you as you develop an evidence-based birth plan and prepare for parenthood.\\nI will be present for your entire birth, supporting you emotionally, mentally, and physically while advocating on your behalf to ensure you have an empowering and beautiful birth experience.\\nBecoming a parent is wonderful, exciting, and challenging. I will be there to support you as you heal and reflect on your birth experience, and settle into life with your newborn.\\n3 prenatal visits, unlimited text & email support, 24/7 on-call period from 38 weeks, continuous support during labor, 1 postpartum home visit, referrals to parenting and breastfeeding/chestfeeding support groups.\\nAnytime you need something but don\\'t want to become mired in the Google rabbit hole, I\\'ll provide you with personalized recommendations for lactation support, childbirth ed, new parents groups, or anything else you\\'re looking for.\\nI offer you the option of documenting your birth experience and the first few moments after your little one is born at no additional charge. This can be done using my camera or one that you provide, though I always bring a polaroid along to provide you with a couple keepsakes.\\nMy standard birth package fee is $2000 total, and my standard postpartum hourly rate is $40/hr. I also offer postpartum overnights at $50/hr.\\nFinal rates are based on a sliding scale.\\nYour personalized fee will be determined by individual circumstances and the services you select.\\nEveryone deserves a doula, so don\\'t let financial concerns stop you from reaching out.\\nPayment plans, trades, and barters are also available upon request.\\nContact me with any questions you may have, or to set up your free consultation so we can find a plan that works for you and your budget.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-25 02:37:49', 'url': 'https://doulakeelia.com/'}\n",
