      "{'text': 'An investigation is continuing into a series of allegations arising out of a misconduct case against a Devon councillor.\\nThe accusations were made during a hearing into the behaviour of Torbay Council member Mark King following a complaint.\\nThe council has confirmed that an investigation launched after the misconduct case last year is still going on.\\nThe council issued a censure against the councillor in October - a statement criticising his behaviour - after he was found to have breached the members’ code of conduct.\\nThe sub-committee which considered the case also asked for new allegations made by the complainant to be investigated.\\nThey included the behaviour of another councillor, the award of contracts for bus services, security, and an event, and planning matters.\\nParts of the allegations are still being investigated, a spokesperson for the council said.\\nCllr King was accused of multiple breaches of the code in his professional capacity as a member of the council’s executive.\\nThe complaint was from a woman Cllr King developed a personal relationship with.\\nThe standards hearing sub-committee last year cleared Cllr King on parts of the complaint.\\nCllr King denied the allegations of wrongdoing against him and refused to accept the findings. He claimed it was a political decision not backed up by evidence.\\nHe has since confirmed he is living in Manila in The Philippines and has no immediate plans to return to the UK, saying he fears for his safety because of an online campaign of bullying and harassment.\\nHe has said he will not be standing for re-election at the local council elections in May.\\nCllr King was elected as a Conservative in 2015 for Cockington with Chelston and put in charge of planning, transport, housing and waste.\\nHe left the Tory group a year ago after a disagreement with the leadership and joined the Liberal Democrats.\\nHe resigned from the Lib-Dems during the disciplinary process in September and went back to being an Independent.\\nHe is still receiving his councillor&apos;s allowance and says he is dealing with issues in his council ward.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-24 20:18:54', 'url': 'https://www.devonlive.com/news/devon-news/investigation-continues-allegations-involving-devon-2709255'}\n",
      "{'text': \"The C3 Basic is the new generation flip-front helmet. It stands out from the crowd at all times through its advanced aerodynamics and pleasing riding characteristics. The positioning of the pad system can be adjusted, enabling fast and easy adaptation of in-helmet head ventilation according to season, weather and preference.\\nMade with Schuberth's S.T.R.O.N.G. fibre and carbon for a lightweight, durable helmet, the C3 combines excellent protection with an aerodynamically optimal shape. The innovative interior lining is outstanding due to its excellent fit and the optimised ventilation and extraction system. The Coolmax pad system is removable and washable with an optimized fit. The helmet comes with an integrated sun visor which can be quickly and easily adjusted with gloves on. The C3 Basic incorporates an effective and powerful ventilation system which enables up to seven litres of fresh air to be supplied per second when travelling at 60mph. Schuberth's 360 Reflex gives the helmet superior visibility and enhanced safety in the dark, with reflective panels visible at every angle.\", 'timestamp': '2019-04-21 04:29:34', 'url': 'https://www.bikestop.co.uk/schuberth-c3-basic-helmet-white'}\n",
