      "{'text': 'So, again to the question. Is it moral? My answer was, ?usually, sure?. three. Search for alternatives where waste may be decreased and re-used as these methods are usually no-cost or low-value. E.g. print paperwork double-sided. So in other phrases, individuals don?t join your company, they join YOU!\\nHave a service mentality: Please additionally learn this tiny article If your code of ethics is five years old or even older, it’s time to reevaluate and evaluation it intimately. Now I’m not referring to your code of conduct. A code of conduct is a compliance doc and is not really thought-about a code of ethics.\\nUntil there are Cayman accounts concerned which Decide Feldman has not confessed too; this amount is hardly price risking his profession over. The only means that Judge Feldman may gain advantage from this choice is politically when it comes to gaining political favors or future campaign donations which might be potential as a result of entrenched oil dependent mentality of the Gulf Coast. ??A lot of these living on the Gulf concern that a persistant deep water ban may improve their states unemployemnt charge by urging BP and other oil producers to relocate to areas possessing loser environmental regualtions.\\nOur network of web sites have the company name on the footer of the site and lots of link monkeys ship the same mail about totally different websites and waste my time when they could have just seemed to see which company it is and make an observation of it so you don?t ship me the same mail again particularly after I reply to them saying to not hassle me again.\\nAustin Mitchell, Labor MP who additionally sits on the Public Accounts Committee, that has to watch public spending on behalf of the Parliament, was of the view that Gauke was himself being unnecessarily moralistic and should higher deal with giant-scale tax avoidance.\\n52 year old Transport Engineer Jarvis from McCreary, has numerous pursuits which include house brewing, . and consuming out. Discovers the beauty in planing a trip to places around the globe, of late only returning from Historic Centre of Mexico City and Xochimilco.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-22 00:26:03', 'url': 'http://fashionjewelrya.us/thorn-finance-nz.html'}\n",
      "{'text': 'Swindon Town Football In The Community Trust are excited to announce that Mike Wood Tyres of Devizes have kindly offered to sponsor the playing kit and equipment for the clubs under 17 girls team. They have now been kitted out in the latest adidas travel suits and playing kits to compete in the world’s largest youth tournament the Gothia Cup. Nearly 1600 teams will be taking part in all age groups from 73 different countries, the Swindon Town FITC team will have to overcome 93 other teams to win the prestigious cup.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-22 12:32:03', 'url': 'https://stfitc.co.uk/?p=937'}\n",
      "{'text': 'My method works for me, but others have different approaches. In her book Debt-Proof Living, author Mary Hunt suggests a sort of “emergency fund plus“. Often when people struggle with money, she says, it’s not the predictable monthly bills that are the problem. People cannot cope with the unexpected things — not just emergencies (like a severe illness), but irregular expenses like auto maintenance, wedding and birthday gifts, or a new pair of shoes.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-18 15:13:56', 'url': 'https://blog.wolffmyren.com/2008/05/12/get-rich-slowly-use-a-freedom-account-to-prepare-for-the-unexpected/'}\n",
      "{'text': 'He completes me... AND completes the painting I couldn\\'t get myself to climb to. Teamwork is essential to take on the homes we have renovated. That and late night projects when our kids are supposed to be in bed and we are wiped out but must continue on. That\\'s the \"we are crazy\" part.\\nGLOSSARY OF PAINT TERMINOLOGY. Paint experts often use terms that make very little sense to the average person, but knowing what these mean will help you make the right choice when it comes to choosing paint colours: (1) COLOUR AND HUE. This refers to the general appearance of a colour and the way it reflects light. (2) TONE. The tone of a colour is a lighter or darker version of a particular colour. (3) TINT AND SHADE. Tint is a lighter version of a colour that is achieved by adding white, while shade is a darker version of a colour achieved by adding black. (4) WARM OR COOL COLOURS. Warm colours are from the red spectrum of a colour wheel, and cool colours are from the blue spectrum of a colour wheel. Rooms that receive a lot of natural light may get hotter than rooms that are south-facing, and this will determine whether you need to select cool or warm colours. (5) NEUTRAL COLOURS. You won’t find neutral colours on a colour wheel as, strictly speaking, these colours are whites, black and grey tones, and brown hues. (6) SHEEN. Sheen refers to the glossiness of a paint finish and the higher the sheen, the glossier the finish. Gloss paints reflect the most light, while matt or flat paints reflect the least.\\nWhen painting in the letters, I spray a coat of poly over the area first and let it dry. This seals the pores and reduces the amount of paint needed to fill in, while also aiding in building up the coats of paint if needed. It also makes removing the excess paint from the surface easier. I tape off larger sections to further reduce the ‘sanding cleanup’ too.\\nThis paint or that paint? Have you ever been to a paint store and your head just wants to explode because it doesn’t make sense why there’s so many of each color?? I took a college course on colors. It was an entire semester on “color”, crazy but so informative. There’s a tone in each color.. warm or cold. You’ll want to consider what feeling you’re trying to create in the space. For example, for my house in Bend, Oregon.. I picked out 2 whites with some warm tones. It’s cold 🥶 here, VERY cold in the winter. So I’m going to stay away from the whites with some blue tones. . Which did you like? Top or bottom?\\nGrays to match the gloomy weather outside today. These our the main 70% colors for our home with #firststar being over half that. First star is super close to white but still has pigment and depth. The other two grays are used sporadically to break up rooms and give new stimuli to the brain as you move through the house. The human brain sees beauty, or is most attracted to, a color scheme break down like the following: 70% a base color (usually a neutral like white, gray, beige but can be a color), 20% a main accent, and 10% another accent, or multiples but they all have to equal only 10% as to not overwhelm the amount of stimuli. We have 70% gray / 20% dark blues / and then the 10% varies with the room we\\'re in but all colors work in tandem together.\\nFinally some cooler weather here in the Hunter Valley that\\'s been perfect for some cleaning before I start my next project. So I thought I\\'d share my favourite cleaning product vanilla metho it\\'s my go to cleaner for everything from my paint brushes, colour mixing pots, mirrors/glass to paint spills on my laminate floor 😑 sadly doesn\\'t smell like vanilla but is a lot more pleasant smelling then regular metho👍 what\\'s your favourite cleaning product?', 'timestamp': '2019-04-22 00:50:57', 'url': 'https://imguram.com/tag/painttips'}\n",
