      "{'text': 'Piper Jane’s nursery is taking much longer than I anticipated (she is almost one already!)… Today I thought I’d share a few of the projects I’m working on and a couple sneak peaks as well!\\nThose geography cards are another current fave.\\nps- This is the first glimpse of Piper Jane’s almost done room! End-of-September is my self imposed finish up deadline- can’t wait to show you the finished room!\\nBeautiful! Love all the possibilities with the new paint, I would probably have at least 17 projects as well :)!\\nWow!! I totally love this new product. Martha always is on trend. Your daughter\\'s room is adorable.\\nOh my word Kirstin it is looking AMAZING. Seriously. Completely in love.\\nI love this idea! Where did you get the flashcards?\\nno way this is darling. i really am just dying right now looking at everything. i want to pin all the pictures!! that spray painting stuff is AWESOME!\\nthanks for sharing. adorable little babies.\\nWow, I didn\\'t know that spray painting kits existed, and YES I looked for coral spray paint for FOUR long months before giving up and moving on… Man I love the color you came up with and will have to ask for a spray painting kit for Christmas so I can finally make myself a coral belt!\\nWow, I didn\\'t know that spray painting kits existed! And YES I search for FOUR months for coral spray paint. Why don\\'t they sell that color? Anyway your color is gorgeous and I found something to add to my Christmas list! THANKS for sharing!\\nHey Georgia! Of course you noticed the cards. 🙂 I love that.\\nI REALLY wanted travel-themed flash cards and couldn\\'t find any, so I just made them. The places are all special to our family (aka- we\\'ve been there, friends live there, we\\'re planning to go there, etc.).\\nOMG! I love what you\\'ve made & of course your color choice! I can\\'t wait to see all the other projects you have in store for us!\\nBeautiful! I love it! I saw something similar on pinterest and was working on my own version in my head, but seeing yours…I am SOOOOO copying! Oh, btw…soo jealous! That set is ah-mazing! I know you\\'ll have a blast with it! Hope you share some more ideas for it soon!\\nwhy a lovely color you blended up! fantastic work!\\nI\\'m looking to add something like this to a window I just got. where did you get the wire/clips to attach to the wood window?\\nYour nursery is SO cute!! I love the colors. And that alphabet board and monogram are so pretty!\\nBTW, the project is SUPER cute and Piper Jane\\'s room is looking great!\\nHey Carmen! There is an \"etching\" add-in that makes the paint stay on ceramics. We used the paints (and the etching stuff) on the elephant shower favors and have put them through the dishwasher a ton and it\\'s held up really well.\\nYou made those Alphabet cards? They are amazing!! May I ask how and where you got the graphics?\\nHey Beckie! Thanks for the compliment- I made them using a couple dingbat map fonts actually. Hope that helps!\\nI love the alphabet cards!\\nHi there. I LOVE the geography flash cards in this room. Would you be willing to share where you purchased these cards? They would be perfect for the nursery we’re preparing. My husband and I are in the process of adopting our first little one!!\\nHey Amanda- CONGRATULATIONS! We are adopting too! Where are you adopting from???\\nI made those flash cards (long, lo-ong ago). I wish I still had access to the files, but my hard drive crashed and I lost them. Sorry that’s not more helpful- I’d totally email them over if I still had the file.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-22 22:22:35', 'url': 'http://kojo-designs.com/2011/09/martha-stewart-decorative-paint-line-and-a-nursery-decor-tutorial/'}\n",
      "{'text': 'TNUSRB Police Constable Result 2017: Hello friends Tamil Nadu police constable exam result 2017 has been announced today on 5 July 2017 on the official website tnusrbonline.org. Tamil Nadu Uniform Service Recruitment Board(TNUSRB) has organises the TNUSRB Exams annually.\\nCandidates who are affiliated to TNUSRB can check their TN Police Constable results 2017 from the official website tnusrbonline.org /tn.gov.in. We would like to suggest all the aspirants to carry their login credentials like registration number and password to check their TNUSRB results 2017.\\nHello friends we would like to advise Candidates to download the TNUSRB merit list 2017 along with the TNUSRB results. Candidates who have managed to get their names in the merit list are allowed to proceed further to the next stage of the process i.e. counselling and personal interviews. The next phase of the interview is physical test followed by the personal interview.\\nA mammoth number of candidates attempts these TN Group II exams but only few of them get a chance to crack these exams and forth into further process. Through these results, applicants will have the opportunity to be placed in the Special Force Group II cadres – Constable, Fireman and Jail Warder. Nearly 5.80 candidates have attempted the TNUSRB exam at 410 exam centers.\\nThe TNUSRB cutoff marks depends upon the post and category of the applicant. The cutoff for general category is 54% and for the reserved category is between 40% to 45%. The aspirants belonging to BCM group has 32% cut off, and MBC category has 48% cutoff. All the above-given TNUSRB cutoffs may vary, so applicants are requested to take it for reference only.\\nIf you liked our article kindly share it on all the social media platforms like whatsapp, facebook, twitter, google plus, flipboard, pinterest, flickr etc.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-23 15:58:51', 'url': 'http://www.timetabledatesheetresults.co.in/results/tnusrb-police-constable-results.html'}\n",
