      "{'text': 'Brian Reed is chair and professor of English at the University of Washington, Seattle. He is the author of three books, most recently Nobody’s Business: Twenty-First Century Avant-Garde Poetics (Cornell University Press, 2013), and the coeditor of two essay collections, Situating El Lissitzky: Vitebsk, Berlin, Moscow (Getty Publications, 2003) and Modern American Poetry: Points of Access (Universitätsverlag Winter, 2013). A new book, A Mine of Intersections: Writing the History of Contemporary Poetry is forthcoming from the University of New Mexico Press.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-21 10:49:57', 'url': 'http://jacket2.org/content/brian-reed'}\n",
