      "{'text': 'Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Opening and Ending singles.\\nI was planning to skip this anime from the very start, but now that everybody is fangirling over it, I just couldn’t leave it like that. What discouraged me at first was the genre. The only Mahou-shoujo anime I can stand is Sailor moon, because I was watching it throughout my whole childhood. BUT. After some time, I decided to get a glimpse of the OP and ED sequences, and I liked them. So, finally, I watched the 1st episode yesterday night, and I liked it. I’m certainly not in awe, because the anime is still in ‘that’ genre, but I liked it very much. I would have never thought that Mahou-shoujo could be used and twisted like that, but the experiment turned out really interesting. + the fact, how worn-out and cliche the genre was, in this anime everything’s mixed perfectly. And another factor which pushed me into watching this is the fact, that the composer of Madoka Magica is Yuki Kajiura. I just LOVE her. That is all.\\nDownload the limited edition single from MirrorCreator.\\nWell, as for this album, I liked only the opening sequence theme, actually. It was really emotional, and I find that it reflects Madoka very nicely too(though I still don’t fully know this character ^^”) As for Kimi to Futari, I didn’t like it at all. It had the typical girly pop feel, that I just can not stand. Dreamin’..? It got a too “Naaaaaah..” reaction from me when I heard it. Nothing more to say.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-26 05:37:35', 'url': 'https://katsuragikaeru.wordpress.com/2011/02/21/mahou-shoujo-madoka-magica-op-ed-singles/'}\n",
