      "{'text': \"Instead of navigating traffic to check out dealerships closer to Atlanta, find an affordable and high-quality used Hyundai model here at Hertz Car Sales Stone Mountain. We're conveniently located on the Stone Mountain Highway if you're heading east out of Atlanta, and when you show up, you'll quickly see why more drivers from this area are shopping with Hertz. Beyond the many used Hyundai models and pre-owned vehicles from other brands, we offer a range of unique Hertz benefits that go a long way toward making your next purchase a truly remarkable deal.\\nWhy the focus on our used Hyundai models? Though we feature used cars, trucks and SUVs from many popular automakers, Hyundai's pre-owned offerings here in Stone Mountain deliver a savvy blend of value with safety, technology and efficiency. Getting to and from work in Atlanta or anywhere else here in this area of Georgia is easy with a fuel-sipping used Hyundai Accent, Elantra or Sonata. If your travels require a little more space inside and added capabilities, check out the used Hyundai SUVs like the Tucson, Santa Fe and Santa Fe Sport to see if there's a fit.\\nIt's certainly easy to find a sensible used Hyundai that handles your driving needs and fits within your budget. The easy shopping experience continues here at Hertz Car Sales Stone Mountain, as we make sure you can secure a sensible used car loan with little to no hassle. Speaking of no hassle, consider the value of our Hertz warranty offerings and protection plans available to purchase, as well as the fair and easy trade-in process that helps you secure a fair rate back for your older car you're selling back to us.\\nSee more of our used Hyundai offerings here at Hertz Car Sales Stone Mountain by coming over today.\", 'timestamp': '2019-04-18 17:02:50', 'url': 'https://www.hertzcarsales.com/stone-mountain/used-cars/hyundai.htm'}\n",
      "{'text': 'A couple of weeks ago we reached the heady stage of planting out Nancy Nightingale’s new border. We laid the specimens in position, carefully considering potential clashes of colour or foliage before we commenced. As NN is a complete novice I gave her a quick planting tutorial before retreating to a safe distance for her to continue unhindered by my critical eye. “What do you think?” she asked after her first attempt. The plant was 1cm proud of the top of the soil. “It isn’t deep enough” I said. To my horror she then curled her hand and thumped the plant down with her fist. “Don’t punch the plants Nancy!” I cried. We then fell about laughing. I explained that the accepted technique is to carefully dig it back up, make a larger hole and try again.\\nLater she messaged me to say that she had made a formal apology to the geum and given it some extra water to make up for “their little misunderstanding”.\\nI’ve got my work cut out here.\\nBrilliant! I have a feeling that ‘potential clashes of colour’ might be quite welcome in this particular garden.\\nDarn it, we should have done that. No need for any violence then!\\nPunching the plants in- oh dear, you’ ve got your work cut out here.\\nIt is a different approach …..\\nI’ve been waiting for an update on Nancy’s garden! She’s caught the bug now and I’m sure she’ll develop into a fine gardener.\\nI think you are right. She loves colour which is a great start.\\nA little in the same mode as ‘Grow yer booger’, a little hardship followed by some TLC has been known to work, from personal experience. Have a great Easter.', 'timestamp': '2019-04-26 16:49:17', 'url': 'https://offtheedgegardening.com/2017/04/15/things-i-never-thought-id-say-part-seven/'}\n",
