      "{'text': \"My 116 bill is past due. (2 phone bill). My spending limit is 450.00. $129, it says has been used. They gave me 6 days to pay the past due. Will my services be cut off even though I have enough to. Cover the bill?\\nGood morning. The spending limit is put in place to make sure that you're bill isn't going over a certain amount. You're still responsible for paying your bill every month and we can interrupt your services due to non payment. This doesn't allow you to spend the full $450 before your services are interrupted, it's just a way to help you monitor your spending.\\nOK I think sprint customer service people need to be on the same page I have two people from sprint telling me different things. My phones and accts were turned off and suspended bc of 125.00 past due and I have a 400 spending limit. 139 was already used it says. **bleep**.\\nHey. The spending limit is put in place to make sure that you're bill isn't going over a certain amount. You're still responsible for paying your bill every month and we can interrupt your services due to non payment. This doesn't allow you to spend the full $400 before your services are interrupted, it's just a way to help you monitor your spending.\", 'timestamp': '2019-04-25 04:42:50', 'url': 'https://community.sprint.com/t5/Payments/Account-Spending-Limit/td-p/1016500'}\n",
      "{'text': 'Physical Therapy is all about movement. The students in the Physical Therapist Assistant program this year have several musically talented people in their cohort. During lab or downtime, they like to play music from their iPods while they work. They also have had to create exercise routines for clients that they have put to music to help the clients keep in rhythm and get their heart rates up.\\nI am asking each student to pick a song that they like that is their “theme song” for getting through the program. I will be combining them onto a CD that I can play for them when music is called for. When they are having a rough week or grinding out a long study session, they will have lots of motivational, inspirational songs to sing them through the blues. I plan to give them each a copy of the CD for graduation in the Spring, so that they will always remember the music of their days as student PTA’s.\\nWe do this in leadership classes all the time but never thought of it for the classroom. GREAT idea, especially for the musical learners!', 'timestamp': '2019-04-19 22:58:03', 'url': 'https://spark.nwtc.edu/2013/12/06/whats-your-theme/'}\n",
